  "skip_reason": "Layer-A canonical drive of `divergence_arakawa_c` requires ESS `discretize`/`parse_rule` to dispatch the FV `applies_to` + `stencil` schema (kind=arakawa selectors at face_x/face_y staggers, axis $x/$y, offsets {0, 1}, with per-row `coeff` AST). ESS `rule_engine.jl::parse_rule` today only consumes the `pattern` + `replacement` schema (E_RULE_REPLACEMENT_MISSING raised on stencil-form rules), so the catalog rule cannot be materialized end-to-end via the canonical pipeline yet. The legacy hand-pinned fixture previously committed here (rule/grid/fields/operator format with a 2x2 cartesian base + dx=dy=0.5 worked example) was a pre-canonical-pipeline regression artifact; ESS does not consume that schema either and Layer-A was FAILing through the n_fail dynamic absorption in test_esd_walker.jl. Once ESS gains stencil-schema dispatch, this stub can be promoted to a hand-pinned canonical contract on the same 2x2 worked example: ux sampled from u(x,y)=x at face_x positions, uy sampled from v(x,y)=y^2 at face_y positions, expected div_F = [[1.5, 2.5], [1.5, 2.5]] at cell centers.",
